  "final_message": "The root cause is a sign error in `mrr` in `billing/reports.py`. It accumulated each subscription's monthly amount with `-`, so every positive amount came out negative.\n\n**Fix:** in `billing/reports.py`, `mrr()` now uses `+` instead of `-` when adding `monthly_amount(...)` to the per-currency total.\n\n**Checked:**\n- `monthly_amount` is correct for your example. The yearly 120.00 USD price becomes 10.00/month, so 30.00 + 10.00 = 40.00 USD.\n- I added `tests/test_reports.py`, which covers that exact monthly + yearly scenario and expects `{\"usd\": 4000}`.\n- Full suite: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` \u2192 25 passed (the 24 existing tests plus the new one).\n- I did not run the new test against the unfixed code to confirm it fails there. The sign flip makes that result clear, but I haven't demonstrated it.\n\n**Answer file:** `answer.json` in the repo root contains `{\"file\": \"reports.py\", \"function\": \"mrr\"}`.\n\nNothing has been committed.",
